# URL of the sterling-vance-api backend (see the ../sterling-vance-api project)
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://localhost:4000/api

# The public URL this site is actually reachable at — used to build the
# sitemap (app/sitemap.ts), robots.txt (app/robots.ts), canonical URLs,
# Open Graph tags and structured data. Set this to your real domain once
# you deploy (e.g. https://www.efcauditing.com); everything falls back to
# http://localhost:3000 if it's left unset, which is fine for local dev
# but wrong for anything search engines see.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=http://localhost:3000

# Cloudinary configuration has moved to the API (Admin → Cloudinary
# Settings, or CLOUDINARY_CLOUD_NAME/CLOUDINARY_API_KEY/CLOUDINARY_API_SECRET
# in sterling-vance-api's own .env as a fallback) — this frontend project no
# longer needs its own Cloudinary env vars at all. lib/cloudinary.ts now asks
# the API for a short-lived signed-upload payload (POST
# /media/cloudinary-signature) instead of holding the secret itself.
